From 955b58b0b6fe2ac520da6fc1a0e05c82e1ec6824 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:20:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Hetzner Cloud as a third Cloud VPS provider

Account connect via a single API token (Hetzner has no dedicated "who am
I" endpoint, so login is validated with a cheap /servers read that also
reports the project's server count).

Server management mirrors UpCloud/Azure: list/view/start/stop/restart,
delete, rebuild (reinstall OS from the server's own current image,
restoring its prior power state), and resize (plan change, gated on the
server being off like UpCloud). Creation wizard: location -> server type
(curated shortlist, filtered per-location by each type's own pricing
data) -> image (curated names resolved against the project's own image
catalog) -> hostname -> auth method (password, auto-generated by Hetzner
itself; or SSH key, registered as its own resource with idempotent
lookup-by-content since Hetzner rejects duplicate key uploads) ->
confirm. Floating IPs: add/remove, using Hetzner's own semantics where
removing an IP deletes it outright (no separate detach step).

Hetzner Cloud API v1 is asynchronous like Azure ARM -- POST responses
return an action that must be polled to a terminal status, handled in
bot/services/hetzner_api.py the same way azure_api.py already does for
Azure. Country flags come straight from Hetzner's own /locations
response (no manual region->country table needed, unlike Azure).
Extensive UI code (keyboards, generic plan-change/must-stop texts) is
reused as-is from the existing UpCloud/Azure implementation.

Deferred for a later round: firewalls, block storage/volumes, server
snapshots/backups, private networks and load balancers.

Verified against a fake Hetzner Cloud API server covering: wrong-token
rejection, per-location server-type/image availability filtering,
SSH-key upload idempotency, multi-poll action resolution (proving the
polling loops actually loop, not just check once), create/start/stop/
reboot/rebuild/resize/delete, and floating IP add/remove -- at both the
service layer and the full Telegram handler layer (wizard state
transitions, stored-password lifecycle, must-stop gating). Also re-ran
the full existing Azure/UpCloud/Happ regression suite to confirm no
breakage.

